Just Cause 3 makes no apologies for it's  outrageous nature it's a power fantasy  in every sense of the phrase placing you  in a world ripe with destructible  environments and giving you instruments  with which to destroy them  there are intermittent technical  problems and scripted moments to track  from the freedom found elsewhere but in  the end Just Cause 3 presents a  spectacular sandbox experience the plot  revolves around returning protagonist  Rico Rodriguez who's arrived in the  fictional Republic of Medici during the  height of a military dictatorship the  story here is forgettable but it  delivers an effective invitation dozens  of military installations cover the  world map and it's your job to blow them  up for the rebel forces Rodriguez  himself is a mash-up of masculine action  stars and comic book characters so it  makes sense that I often feel like a  superhero in his shoes by supplying us  with a wingsuit parachute and grappling  hook Just Cause 3 gives us not just  effective means of transportation but  also a smooth nuanced traversal system  there is a steep learning curve but with  practice I was leaping from helicopters  gliding through enemy bases and floating  over farmland with ease I actually felt  like a hero learning his new skill set  it's as if Avalanche Studios combined  Batman spider-man and The Punisher and  thrust its creation into a vivid  Mediterranean landscape what follows is  a kaleidoscope of spectacle and scale  helicopters dot the sky chain explosions  cover the screen in a world teetering  toward total destruction Just Cause 3  grants us the tools to push it over the  edge I have the traditional grenades  remote mines and numerous land air and  sea vehicles on call but then there's  the tether this grappling hook  modification attaches to separate  objects and through tension can pull  them toward each other with hilarious  results I reeled enemies toward  explosive barrels collapse watchtowers  and pulled attack helicopters into a  fiery end  it's a testament to this game's  creativity that guns were often my last  resort like Olive Just Cause threes best  moments the tether encourages  experimentation rather than thoughtless  reaction and as the hours passed the  destruction stayed fresh the small  mechanic encapsulate what makes Just  Cause 3 so fun it leads to numerous  possibilities and even now after 30  hours in this idyllic sandbox I'm sure I  haven't seen them all and almost every  activity in Just Cause threes world is  worth doing as you liberate new  provinces from enemy hands  challenges will pop up across the map  these include vehicle races machine guns  score contests and wingsuit dives and by  completing these you'll unlock new gear  mods which further change the function  of certain items while some of these are  miners such as increased grenade  capacity or a nitrous boost for vehicles  others reveal dynamic new ways to  experiment in Just Cause threes world  take the booster mod for remote mines  for example whereas previous versions of  the device just detonated at a chosen  time this modification sends objects  careening into distant structures before  exploding I use this on cars numerous  times creating two-ton bombs that flew  toward enemy fuel tanks after I have  dough from the driver's seat and this is  only one of the many uses I discovered  with just this one small upgrade this  cascading structure is what makes Just  Cause 3 so great there's a cadence to  how you approach its world outpost  liberation leads to challenges which  lead to gear mods which lead to even  further experimentation and more often  than not each tier of this formula is  entertaining in itself Just Cause 3  excels because it adds variety to the  equation throughout making destruction  and mayhem entertaining far past the  early hours however Just Cause 3 does  deviate from its open-world freedom at  times and what it does it falters the  scripted story missions progress the  plot but the actual gameplay involved is  repetitive at best and broken at worst  the vast majority of these tasks are  escort missions in which you defend a  plane or boat or caravan of jeeps  protecting another character can be  tiresome to begin with but when their  behavior is unpredictable and often  unintelligent I restarted checkpoints  far more than felt fair just cos 3 is  also filled with some bugs and other  rough edges my parachute sometimes  closed at random and AI behavior made  several story objectives impossible  and for a game that places death front  and center it was often inconsistent  with whether I should die or not I'm  happy just cause 3 is lenient with its  falling damage considering I'm in the  sky more often than not when I survived  a 500-foot fall at one point only to die  from a shorter one soon thereafter these  mishaps would be easy to overlook if  they didn't disrupt an otherwise fluid  experience too often when Just Cause 3  is consistent however it's a stunning  display of cause and effect but there's  a more thoughtful undercurrent as well  despite the explosions and instant  gratification throughout Just Cause 3  also encourages experimentation and  foresight and the results are as  rewarding as they are entertaining
 

